You are working in D:\PRISM-ui-fixes on branch `ui/fixes-and-extras`. Apply the following UI fixes for the PRISM dashboard, then build and commit. Do NOT push to remote.

## Tasks

### 1. Remove side edge borders from panels
In these files, remove `borderLeft` and `borderRight` from top-level `aside`/panel containers (the outer edge borders):
- `frontend/src/components/LeftPanel.tsx` (line 12): remove `borderRight: "1px solid var(--border)", borderLeft: "1px solid var(--border)"`
- `frontend/src/components/RightPanel.tsx` (line 33): remove `borderLeft: "1px solid var(--border)", borderRight: "1px solid var(--border)"`
- `frontend/src/components/BottomPanel.tsx` (line 77): remove `borderLeft: "1px solid var(--border)", borderRight: "1px solid var(--border)"` from the outer panel
- `frontend/src/App.tsx` (line 35): remove `borderLeft: "1px solid var(--border)", borderRight: "1px solid var(--border)"` from `.prism-map` div
- `frontend/src/components/TopBar.tsx` (line 36): remove `borderLeft: "1px solid var(--border-strong)"` from the subtitle span
- Keep internal section dividers (between TopBar sections) — those are fine

### 2. Make vehicles and routes larger and more visible
In `frontend/src/components/MapView.tsx` around line 339-356, find the `prism-png-shadow`, `prism-png-dot`, `prism-png-layer` layers:
- `prism-png-shadow` `circle-radius`: `5` → `8`, `circle-translate`: `[2, 4]` → `[3, 6]`
- `prism-png-dot` `circle-radius`: `3.5` → `5`
- `prism-png-layer` `icon-size`: `0.06` → `0.12`

In `frontend/src/map/layers/routeLayer.ts`:
- `prism-route-shadow` `line-width`: `7` → `9`, `line-opacity`: `0.18` → `0.25`
- `prism-route-remaining` `line-width`: `3.5` → `4.5`, `line-opacity`: `0.9` → `1.0`, `line-dasharray`: `[2, 2]` → `[1.5, 1.5]`

### 3. Add severity tooltip on incident hover
In `frontend/src/components/MapView.tsx`:
- Add a state `const [hoverIncident, setHoverIncident] = useState<{id: string; title: string; severity: string; event_type: string; people: number; priority: number; x: number; y: number} | null>(null)`
- Add event listeners after the ward click handlers (around line 410-430):
```ts
map.on("mousemove", "incidents-circle", (e: maplibregl.MapLayerMouseEvent) => {
  if (!e.features?.[0]) return;
  const p = e.features[0].properties as Record<string, unknown>;
  setHoverIncident({
    id: String(p.id),
    title: String(p.title),
    severity: String((incidentsRef.current.find(i=>i.id===String(p.id))?.severity) ?? "moderate"),
    event_type: String(incidentsRef.current.find(i=>i.id===String(p.id))?.summary ?? "—"),
    people: incidentsRef.current.find(i=>i.id===String(p.id))?.reports ?? 0,
    priority: Number(p.priority) || 0,
    x: e.point.x,
    y: e.point.y,
  });
  map.getCanvas().style.cursor = "pointer";
});
map.on("mouseleave", "incidents-circle", () => {
  setHoverIncident(null);
  map.getCanvas().style.cursor = "";
});
```
- In the JSX (right after the existing `hoverAsset` tooltip, around line 905), add:
```tsx
{hoverIncident && (
  <div style={{
    position: "absolute",
    left: Math.min(hoverIncident.x + 14, 520),
    top: Math.min(hoverIncident.y + 14, 420),
    background: "rgba(8,12,14,0.98)",
    border: `1px solid ${hoverIncident.severity === "critical" ? "rgba(255,77,77,0.4)" : hoverIncident.severity === "high" ? "rgba(245,185,66,0.4)" : "rgba(72,216,255,0.4)"}`,
    borderLeft: `2px solid ${hoverIncident.severity === "critical" ? "#FF4D4D" : hoverIncident.severity === "high" ? "#F5B942" : "#48D8FF"}`,
    borderRadius: 4, padding: "8px 9px", pointerEvents: "none", zIndex: 6, minWidth: 220,
    boxShadow: "0 10px 28px rgba(0,0,0,0.55)",
  }}>
    <div className="mono" style={{ fontSize: 9, fontWeight: 800, letterSpacing: "0.08em", color: "var(--text)" }}>{hoverIncident.title}</div>
    <div className="mono" style={{ fontSize: 8, color: hoverIncident.severity === "critical" ? "#FF4D4D" : hoverIncident.severity === "high" ? "#F5B942" : "#48D8FF", fontWeight: 800, letterSpacing: "0.1em", marginTop: 4 }}>SEVERITY {hoverIncident.severity.toUpperCase()}</div>
    <div className="mono" style={{ fontSize: 9, color: "var(--text-muted)", marginTop: 4, lineHeight: 1.4 }}>
      Type: {hoverIncident.event_type} • Reports: {hoverIncident.people} • Priority: {hoverIncident.priority}
    </div>
  </div>
)}
```

### 4. Verify vehicle hover tooltip exists
Check around line 880-920 of MapView.tsx — there should already be a `hoverAsset` tooltip showing ETA, from/to, etc. Make sure it works on the `prism-png-layer`. If `mousemove`/`mouseleave` for `prism-png-layer` are missing or weak, add them. The existing code at the bottom of the file already has this tooltip.

### 5. Add signal-loss city highlight (pulsing yellow overlay on Wards 33/41/57)
In `frontend/src/components/MapView.tsx`, after the wards-fill layer is added (around line 70-90), add:

```ts
// Signal-loss cities — pulsing yellow/amber highlight on silent wards
const signalLossGeo = {
  type: "FeatureCollection",
  features: [
    { type: "Feature", properties: { ward: "33" }, geometry: { type: "Polygon", coordinates: [[[91.66, 26.13],[91.69, 26.13],[91.69, 26.16],[91.66, 26.16],[91.66, 26.13]]] } },
    { type: "Feature", properties: { ward: "41" }, geometry: { type: "Polygon", coordinates: [[[91.75, 26.17],[91.78, 26.17],[91.78, 26.20],[91.75, 26.20],[91.75, 26.17]]] } },
    { type: "Feature", properties: { ward: "57" }, geometry: { type: "Polygon", coordinates: [[[91.81, 26.12],[91.84, 26.12],[91.84, 26.15],[91.81, 26.15],[91.81, 26.12]]] } },
  ],
} as unknown as never;
map.addSource("cities-signal-loss", { type: "geojson", data: signalLossGeo });
map.addLayer({
  id: "cities-signal-loss-fill",
  type: "fill",
  source: "cities-signal-loss",
  paint: {
    "fill-color": "#F5B942",
    "fill-opacity": 0.28,
  },
} as unknown as never);
map.addLayer({
  id: "cities-signal-loss-pulse",
  type: "line",
  source: "cities-signal-loss",
  paint: {
    "line-color": "#F5B942",
    "line-width": 2,
    "line-opacity": 0.85,
    "line-dasharray": [3, 2],
  },
} as unknown as never);
```

Then add a pulse animation (after `pngReadyRef.current = true`):
```ts
let pulseT = 0;
const signalLossInterval = setInterval(() => {
  pulseT = (pulseT + 1) % 100;
  const opacity = 0.28 + 0.25 * Math.abs(Math.sin(pulseT * 0.0628));
  if (map.getLayer("cities-signal-loss-fill")) {
    map.setPaintProperty("cities-signal-loss-fill", "fill-opacity", opacity);
  }
}, 80);
```

Save the interval handle so it can be cleared on map unload (find the cleanup section and add `clearInterval(signalLossInterval);`).

### 6. Generalize to all disasters
Search for "flood" or "Flood" in `frontend/src/components/`, `frontend/src/store/`, `frontend/src/data/`, `frontend/src/types/`. Replace flood-specific text with neutral disaster-agnostic wording (e.g., "incident", "disaster event", "response"). Don't remove useful incident data.

### 7. Build & commit
Run `cd D:\PRISM-ui-fixes\frontend && npm run build` and fix any errors. Then:
`git add -A && git commit -m "ui: remove side edge borders, larger vehicles + routes, incident severity hover, signal-loss city highlight, generalize to all disasters"`

## Report back
- List of files changed
- Confirmation that `npm run build` passed (paste the relevant lines)
- The commit hash
- Any issues encountered

